\subsection{Definitions and mathematical statement}
\paragraph{Statement recorded in the supplied source.}
For every finite-dimensional algebra A over a field and every finite-dimensional left A-module M, does $Ext_A^i(M,M\oplus A)=0$ for all integers $i>0$ imply that M is projective?

\subsection{Short English statement}
For every finite-dimensional algebra A over a field and every finite-dimensional left A-module M, does $Ext_A^i(M,M\oplus A)=0$ for all integers $i>0$ imply that M is projective?

\subsection{Sources}
\begin{itemize}
\item[S1] Original question source or mathematical context.
\url{https://doi.org/10.4171/owr/2005/06}.
\item[S2] OpenAI, manuscript citation page. Source of the formulation motivating this local problem.
\url{https://github.com/openai/math/blob/adc7f1241b42e322a6451854ab7e4b4c146bf78a/preprints/An-explicit-counterexample-to-the-Auslander-Reiten-conjecture-September-23-2026/README.md}.
\end{itemize}

